Author: Nxeon <haxkodi@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 14:19:36 2026 +0000

    Paginate the visitor analytics traffic feed

    The date-range traffic feed on /admin/visitors was hard-capped at 200
    rows (FEED_LIMIT) with no way to see anything past that, even though a
    filtered range could legitimately hold more matches. Switch it to real
    server-side pagination using the same paginate()/pageHref() helper and
    25-row page size already used by the invoices and users admin lists.

    visitFeed() now takes skip/take (from paginate()) instead of a flat
    limit. The page renders Prev/Next controls building on the existing
    from/to/kind/dir filter, and TrafficFeedFilter resets page=1 whenever
    a filter is applied so a stale page number can't outlive the filter
    that produced it.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

